<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Pact</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;After a lifetime of loss and trauma, Catra makes a life-changing promise to Bow and Glimmer that no-one ever expected her to make - least of all her girlfriend Adora, who has sacrificed her hopes of motherhood for a childfree life with Catra. Things get messy af.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Non-linear AU in which Catra is Bow and Glimmer's surrogate, and in which the lines between friendship, love, parenthood and survivorship blur. Potential triggering themes include childhood trauma, coming out and internalised homophobia, domestic violence, childbirth, infertility, loss,  physical disfigurement, and exploration of ethnic/racial identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra knitted her eyebrows together, pressing her lips into a thin line. Adora caught her breath in her throat. Sheâ€™d tried to avoid thinking too much about what this would be like, watching Catra in pain. It had been so many years since sheâ€™d seen Catra suffer, at least so visibly. She braced herself to keep focused in the moment, to not think back to the things she wished neither of them had had to live through. But it was so hard when Catraâ€™s pain responses still seemed to look exactly the sameâ€¦&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
